  "prediction": "The report provides an overview of the FY2018 and FY2019 Agriculture appropriations acts and their impact on conservation programs. In FY2018, the appropriations act included amendments to the WFPO program and farm bill conservation programs, exempting them from certain requirements. The FY2019 appropriations act also included policy provisions related to conservation, some of which were carried over from previous years.\n\nDuring the fiscal year 2018-2019, there was a lapse in funding for some federal agencies, including the USDA, which affected the implementation of conservation programs. However, the report notes that NRCS continued to provide financial assistance for conservation practices during the lapse.\n\nThe report also highlights the importance of the Farm Bill in authorizing and funding conservation programs, and the role of the Agriculture appropriations act in providing additional resources and policy guidance. The report concludes by emphasizing the need for continued funding and support for conservation programs to help farmers and ranchers implement practices that promote environmental sustainability and economic viability.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report provides an overview of the FY2018 and FY2019 Agriculture appropriations acts and their impact on conservation programs. In FY2018, the appropriations act included amendments to the WFPO program and farm bill conservation programs, exempting them from certain requirements. The FY2019 appropriations act also included policy provisions related to conservation, some of which were carried over from previous years.\n\nDuring the fiscal year 2018-2019, there was a lapse in funding for some federal agencies, including the USDA, which affected the implementation of conservation programs. However, the report notes that NRCS continued to provide financial assistance for conservation practices during the lapse.\n\nThe report also highlights the importance of the Farm Bill in authorizing and funding conservation programs, and the role of the Agriculture appropriations act in providing additional resources and policy guidance. The report concludes by emphasizing the need for continued funding and support for conservation programs to help farmers and ranchers implement practices that promote environmental sustainability and economic viability.",
